A||N||4||Elenor84||Taking off seat covers without ripping material?||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||08-12-2001||04:24 PM||||Hey guys...sold some seat covers and I want to get them off the seats but I don't want to rip the material...how do I do this?  Thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||varnster||08-12-2001||05:09 PM||||use a set of diagonal cutters, to remove the <BR>hog rings, just start from the bottom and work your way up, their are some rods in the<BR>bottom and the top of the covers just be careful, and take your time.Allso unbolt the<BR>top of the seat from the bottom, and be careful to unload the the spring under the<BR>seat, the one that helps you slide the seat<BR>front to back, you don't want those rails to<BR>smack you in the mouth during disassembly||||reg||14
Z||000002||dpittman||08-12-2001||08:20 PM||||(Since I'm the purchaser)<P>As long as you're careful and the front (visible) portions look decent . . . I won't be complaining.  <P>Of course if I receive a box full of shards that looks like my cat had his way with it, then that would probably be less than satisfactory. :-)<P><BR>David<BR>86/v6/se/4spd/Grey<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Elenor84||08-14-2001||01:58 AM||||David man u can trust me...I have more respect for this seat then I do for my family(j/k)<BR>I love fiero's and I would never harm a part of it!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
